  "semantic_disclosures": [
    "Campaign assignment is not an observed impression or click.",
    "Campaign START_DAY is an ordering proxy, not an observed exposure timestamp.",
    "Attribution is descriptive allocation and must not be interpreted as causal lift.",
    "Attributed Households is non-additive across campaigns.",
    "AOV and UPT are calculated from aggregated attributed values, not averaged row ratios.",
    "Signed source Sales and Units are preserved without clipping.",
    "Raw source QUANTITY is retained as governed evidence but is not presented as conventional UPT because extreme quantity observations dominate the raw total. Attributed Items uses normalized transaction-line count; Items / Order equals Attributed Items divided by Attributed Orders."
